    {
      "name": "set_transfer_vk",
      "docs": [
        "CHUNKED. A TRANSFER_VK_LEN-byte VK plus its accounts, signature and blockhash no longer fits the",
        "1232-byte transaction limit — the fee's eighth IC point is what pushed it over, so this is",
        "a direct consequence of §3a and not an unrelated refactor. Send it in pieces, in order.",
        "",
        "`written` is the guard, not a convenience: a partly-written VK rejects EVERY proof, so a",
        "suite of negative tests stays green while nothing works, and the error says `InvalidProof`",
        "— about the proof, for a defect in the key. That is exactly what the truncated `ic` array",
        "did. Completeness is therefore state the verifying paths check."
      ],
