              }
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "max_fee",
            "docs": [
              "§3a — the largest fee a relayed withdraw/transfer may pay out of the pool, in mint units.",
              "APPENDED, deliberately: every field above keeps its offset, so this is the one Pool change",
              "that a byte-offset reader survives. It does NOT make Pool safe to parse by offset — the",
              "deposit_vk growth above already moved everything after it — but it means the two changes",
              "are separable when someone reconstructs the layout.",
              "",
              "A cap is not a policy choice deferred to the relayer. Without it, a compromised or greedy",
              "relayer names any fee it likes and the circuit happily proves conservation: the user's",
              "balance is conserved into the RELAYER's pocket. Conservation says value is not created; it",
              "says nothing about who receives it."
            ],
            "type": "u64"
          },
          {
            "name": "deposits_paused",
            "docs": [
              "SUNSET SWITCH — closes the ENTRANCE, never the exit. When true, `deposit` is rejected;",
              "`withdraw_with_change` and `transfer` are deliberately NOT gated on it.",
              "",
              "THIS EXISTS BECAUSE IT CANNOT BE ADDED LATER. A superseded pool does not stop being usable",
              "when a newer one is deployed: every installed wallet still pointing at the old program goes",
              "on working against it, without a warning, under whatever key model that program had. On",
              "devnet that is merely untidy. At mainnet the VK — and with it the program — must be",
              "immutable, and immutability removes the ability to add this switch at the moment it is",
              "first needed. \"Abandoned\" is not \"disabled\", and the difference is only decidable while the",
              "program is still upgradeable.",
              "",
              "THE ASYMMETRY IS THE DESIGN. Disabling a pool by zeroing its VKs would also be one",
              "transaction and would also stop deposits — and it would strand every existing note, because",
              "the same verifying key is what lets a holder get their funds OUT. A sunset must close the",
              "entrance and leave the exit open, or it is not a sunset, it is a seizure.",
              "u8, not bool: `bool` is not `Pod`, and a zero-copy account cannot hold a type whose",
              "invalid bit patterns are undefined. 0 = open, non-zero = sunset."
            ],
            "type": "u8"
          },
          {
            "name": "_pad2",
            "type": {
              "array": [
                "u8",
                7
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "RhoMarker",
      "docs": [
        "§2.4.2 — rho uniqueness marker. PDA [\"rho\", rho]. Existence = that rho has been used by a",
        "deposit, so a second deposit reusing it FAILS TO INITIALIZE and the transaction is rejected.",
        "",
        "WHY A WHOLE ACCOUNT FOR A DEPOSITOR'S OWN MISTAKE. `deposit`'s rho is prover-chosen, and two",
        "notes sharing a rho share a nullifier: the second is permanently unspendable, and NOTHING",
        "FAILS AT PROVING TIME. \"It is self-harm, so it is fine\" is the argument this design exists to",
        "reject — silent fund loss is the failure mode, and a rejected transaction is the loud version",
        "of the same event. Carries only the bump, for the same privacy reason as Nullifier."
      ],
      "type": {
        "kind": "struct",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "bump",
            "type": "u8"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
