            "name": "written",
            "docs": [
              "Bytes of `vk` written so far. A VK that no longer fits in ONE transaction has to arrive in",
              "chunks, and a partly-written key is the failure mode this whole review keeps finding: it",
              "rejects every proof, so every negative test passes and the symptom is `InvalidProof` — a",
              "message about the proof, for a defect in the key. Exactly what a truncated `ic` array did",
              "in #35. So completeness is STATE, and the verifying paths require `written == VK_LEN`",
              "before they will look at a proof at all."
            ],
            "type": "u32"
          },
